+# Marginalia Books
+
+A static website for Marginalia Books, a fictional independent bookshop at
+14 Quire Lane, Hollowbrook. It has four pages:
+
+- **Home** introduces the shop and links to the other pages.
+- **Books** is a catalogue of invented titles with a genre filter. The filter
+  lives in the page address (`books.html?genre=mystery`), so it can be
+  bookmarked and works with the browser's back and forward buttons.
+- **Events** lists upcoming events with dates, times and whether booking is
+  needed.
+- **Visit** has opening hours, the address, directions, accessibility
+  information and a contact form. The form is a demo and does not send
+  anything.
+
+The site is plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript with no build step, no frameworks
+and no npm dependencies. It makes no requests outside its own origin.
+
+## Viewing the site
+
+Serve the repository root with any static server, then open the printed
+address. For example, using `http-server` from npm:
+
+```sh
+npx http-server -p 8080 -c-1 .
+```
+
+Then open <http://localhost:8080/>.
+
+## Tests
+
+The tests drive the pages in headless Chrome through Playwright. They serve the
+repository on a free local port, so Playwright must be installed and Chrome
+must be at `/usr/bin/google-chrome`.
+
+```sh
+NODE_PATH=/opt/node22/lib/node_modules node tests/run.mjs
+```
+
+Pass a name fragment to run a subset, for example
+`NODE_PATH=/opt/node22/lib/node_modules node tests/run.mjs c5`.
+
+## Formatting
+
+Every HTML, CSS and JavaScript file is checked with Prettier:
+
+```sh
+npx --no-install prettier --check "**/*.{html,css,js,mjs}"
+```
+
+## Layout
+
+- `index.html`, `books.html`, `events.html`, `visit.html`: the pages.
+- `css/styles.css`: the one stylesheet.
+- `js/main.js`: navigation toggle and footer year, loaded on every page.
+- `js/books.js`: catalogue data and the genre filter.
+- `js/visit.js`: contact form validation.
+- `tests/run.mjs`: browser tests, one or more per acceptance criterion.
